(audience applauding)

3
00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:05.611
All right.

4
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.050
Scarlett, what's your most irrational fear?

5
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.013
My most irrational fear?

6
00:00:13.296 --> 00:00:14.600
Well, I don't know.

7
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.900
I used to be like, I'm never gonna work again.

8
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.770
I would finish a job and then be like, that's it.

9
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.890
Well, I had a good run and I'm never gonna work again.

10
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:23.730
So, yes.

11
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.394
That's a good one.

12
00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:26.540
It's bad, it's not good.

13
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.180
No, but it's understandable and relatable.

14
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.920
Okay, if you could see into the future,

15
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.343
what would you want to know?

16
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.143
I would want to know if Trump is gonna run again.

17
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.400
I just want to know, so I can be prepared.

18
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.150
I'm gonna bet yes.

19
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.950
I feel like that's probably gonna happen.

20
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.550
No.
Well.

21
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.980
I don't know if I can handle it.

22
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.460
I just don't know.

23
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.213
Sorry, I know this is like, a divisive topic.

24
00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:56.680
You would like to mentally prepare yourself.

25
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.080
I need to be mentally prepared, that's all.

26
00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.130
That's all I'll say.

27
00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.110
All right, I get that.

28
00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.060
Okay, what is something that you hope your kids

29
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.140
never find out about you?

30
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.010
I'm supposed to say that?

31
00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.300
Oh yeah, that does defeat the purpose.

32
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.400
I'm trying to think what would I

33
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.309
not want my kids to find out about?

34
00:01:13.309 --> 00:01:14.142
(Drew burps)

35
00:01:14.142 --> 00:01:17.570
I'm sorry, I ate a ton of bugs earlier.

36
00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.660
That was so nasty.

37
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:20.493
I cannot.

38
00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.490
Oh my gosh, it was actually making me sick

39
00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.323
watching you do that.

40
00:01:24.323 --> 00:01:26.310
I have to tell you, they were delicious.

41
00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.750
They needed a little salt.

42
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.880
Other than that, they were great.

43
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.760
There is no possible way I could do that.

44
00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.290
They were really good, actually.

45
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.520
No, no, they weren't.
I swear, I swear.

46
00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.220
I would eat 'em on a salad.

47
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:38.453
Crunch, crunch.
No.

48
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.680
Would you?
Yes, I think I would.

49
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.663
Ugh, no, I can't.

50
00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.100
Okay, what is something your kids-

51
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.670
Oh, you know what I-

52
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.950
Well, I don't know.

53
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.030
My daughter may have asked me this before.

54
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.960
I used to smoke when I was younger,

55
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:55.950
and I'm so like, ashamed.

56
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.590
I just don't want her to ever think

57
00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.460
that I ever thought it was cool,

58
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.410
'cause she can never, ever, ever smoke.

59
00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:03.973
'Cause that's what you do,

60
00:02:03.973 --> 00:02:05.310
you forbid your kids from doing things

61
00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.710
and then they don't do them.

62
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.513
So, yeah.

63
00:02:09.513 --> 00:02:12.700
I just hope she never kind of figures that out.

64
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.050
All right, when are you the most competitive?

65
00:02:16.194 --> 00:02:18.420
I am the most when I'm playing backgammon.

66
00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.370
It's great, I love backgammon.

67
00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.000 line:15%
So Colin and I started playing backgammon

68
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.513 line:15%
a couple of years ago.

69
00:02:26.252 --> 00:02:27.887 line:15%
Somebody had given us a board like,

70
00:02:27.887 --> 00:02:29.660 line:15%
one of our checker boards or something was like,

71
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.110 line:15%
also a backgammon board.

72
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.100 line:15%
Like, I've always wanted to know how you play this game.

73
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.870
It's pretty easy to learn it.

74
00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:38.670
And Colin annoyingly wins-

75
00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.380
He wins at everything and it's so annoying.

76
00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.543
Anyway, it's just like,

77
00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.220
he'll last minute like, roll a bunch of doubles,

78
00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.810
and you're like, why?

79
00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.700
There's no way, like how is this happening?

80
00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:49.583
He's so lucky.

81
00:02:51.342 --> 00:02:53.930
But he also has been playing it on his phone

82
00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.470
and it's like, that's not fair, that's cheating.

83
00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.600
He's picking up all these like,

84
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.840
tools that he would never otherwise have

85
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.840
because he's like, playing on his phone.

86
00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.000
I don't like it.

87
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:04.870
Hm.
I don't like it.

88
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.980
Makes me want to like, find a backgammon champion

89
00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.840
and like, get them to you secretly

90
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.683
so you could like, brush up on tips.

91
00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.650
We'll talk.

92
00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.240
Text you later.

93
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.920
Okay, last question.

94
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.533
Is it true that you can cry on command?

95
00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:22.683
I could try.

96
00:03:25.253 --> 00:03:27.710
I probably could-ish, yeah.

97
00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.026
Okay, want to try?
Yeah.

98
00:03:30.026 --> 00:03:32.408
(Drew sighs)

99
00:03:32.408 --> 00:03:34.500
(audience laughing)

100
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.003
You're going to a dark place.

101
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.940
It's true, I only ever cry

102
00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:44.010
when I start talking about like, my daughters, you know?

103
00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.300
Okay, so you're gonna go there.

104
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.670
I'm gonna go there.
Okay.

105
00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.530
Like, I didn't think that I could-

106
00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.790
I didn't think that I would ever have the opportunity

107
00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.600
to have the experience in life that I didn't have

108
00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.310
with my mom, you know?

109
00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:02.550
And it really just messes me up and it's like a chance

110
00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:10.200
to get things, you know, not right,

111
00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.540
'cause they were never wrong.

112
00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.230
I loved my childhood.

113
00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.340
Wouldn't change it for a thing.

114
00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.290
But it's like, all of a sudden,

115
00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:20.770
I just have this magical ability to-

116
00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.310
I'm still thinking about you.

117
00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.480
I'm like, I'm half there, but I'm half paying attention.

118
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.160
Oh my god, there goes the roll!

119
00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.500
The tear came out.

120
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.333
It came out.

121
00:04:29.333 --> 00:04:30.952
You win.

122
00:04:30.952 --> 00:04:31.785
You win!

123
00:04:31.785 --> 00:04:33.656
(audience applauding)

124
00:04:33.656 --> 00:04:34.489
Full tear.

125
00:04:35.962 --> 00:04:37.795
Full tear out the eye.

126
00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:42.038
(Scarlett speaking indistinctly)

127
00:04:42.038 --> 00:04:44.200
No, but you had them rolling out.

128
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.410
I was on the surface 'cause I'm half in,

129
00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.460
like half paying attention.

130
00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:52.250
Nicely done, Johansson.

131
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.761
Got the roll.

132
00:04:53.761 --> 00:04:56.928
(audience applauding)

133
00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.610
Anybody tuning in right now is gonna be like,

134
00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.283
these people are sociopaths.

135
00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.780
That's every day on this show.

136
00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:10.780
We like to be weird and have fun and get deep.

137
00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.963
It's such a great show, I am so excited for you.

138
00:05:15.098 --> 00:05:17.730
Like, you're where you're supposed to be.

139
00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.488
It's just wonderful.

140
00:05:19.488 --> 00:05:21.767
(audience applauding)

141
00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:23.470
I will say, in all sincerity,

142
00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:26.350
I almost cried when you came out 'cause I was like,

143
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:29.973
proud to show you like, what we've been doing here.

144
00:05:29.973 --> 00:05:32.556
(upbeat music)

